This was the working title of the song.

1321
00:56:12.500 --> 00:56:14.780
So this is what would have been, like, on a script.

1322
00:56:15.080 --> 00:56:18.280
Like, now Jefferson Starship plays this song.

1323
00:56:18.280 --> 00:56:27.920
They changed it to Light the Sky on Fire when they released it, but the working title was, and I can't believe this didn't stick.

1324
00:56:28.280 --> 00:56:32.080
Because it rolls off the tongue.

1325
00:56:32.080 --> 00:56:33.720
It is.

1326
00:56:35.260 --> 00:56:36.300
It is.

1327
00:56:36.460 --> 00:56:38.240
It has parentheses in it.

1328
00:56:38.440 --> 00:56:38.860
It is.

1329
00:56:39.980 --> 00:56:41.760
Cigar-shaped object.

1330
00:56:42.680 --> 00:56:43.440
Parentheses.

1331
00:56:43.760 --> 00:56:45.100
Vanished without a trace.

1332
00:56:46.040 --> 00:56:46.800
What?

1333
00:56:47.160 --> 00:56:50.280
Can you believe that that name didn't stick?

1334
00:56:50.660 --> 00:56:52.260
Cigar-shaped object?

1335
00:56:52.260 --> 00:56:58.020
Cigar-shaped object vanished without a trace, was the original title of the song.

1336
00:56:58.580 --> 00:57:04.900
This appearance marked Marty Balin's final appearance with Jefferson Starship.

1337
00:57:05.580 --> 00:57:08.580
He was one of the members who broke off.

1338
00:57:08.580 --> 00:57:14.620
The lyrics of the song mention a, quote, great god.

1339
00:57:15.020 --> 00:57:16.840
I didn't get the cigar.

1340
00:57:17.380 --> 00:57:19.340
Oh, here, this might be it.

1341
00:57:19.520 --> 00:57:26.220
They mention a great god named Copacan who, quote, came from the stars and vanished.

1342
00:57:26.620 --> 00:57:30.080
So is Copacan cigar-shaped?

1343
00:57:30.520 --> 00:57:32.200
Who is Copacan?

1344
00:57:32.200 --> 00:57:36.240
Do we hear about this person later in Star Wars?

1345
00:57:36.520 --> 00:57:38.360
Not that comes from memory.

1346
00:57:38.580 --> 00:57:39.140
We don't know.

1347
00:57:39.760 --> 00:57:40.320
Okay.

1348
00:57:40.600 --> 00:57:47.320
Well, the version that they played on the special was never released, but a shortened single was released.

1349
00:57:47.880 --> 00:57:54.200
But rather than listen to it, Angela, I would like to instead take you back to the late 80s.

1350
00:57:55.080 --> 00:57:57.300
To your middle school mixer.

1351
00:57:57.620 --> 00:57:58.060
Okay.

1352
00:57:58.400 --> 00:58:02.880
So that we can listen to this song by Jefferson Starship.

1353
00:58:03.400 --> 00:58:04.740
We built this city.

1354
00:58:07.530 --> 00:58:08.290
You're welcome.

1355
00:58:08.710 --> 00:58:11.430
We built this city.

1356
00:58:11.630 --> 00:58:11.990
Mm-hmm.

1357
00:58:18.480 --> 00:58:18.900
All right.

1358
00:58:19.040 --> 00:58:20.160
I'll get up and dance with you.

1359
00:58:35.670 --> 00:58:36.510
That's right.

1360
00:58:38.030 --> 00:58:40.870
Get my high tops with my scrunchie socks.

1361
00:58:41.330 --> 00:58:41.630
Mm-hmm.

1362
00:58:41.890 --> 00:58:42.950
Crimp my hair.

1363
00:58:43.250 --> 00:58:44.830
We needed this palette cleanse.

1364
00:58:44.830 --> 00:58:45.250
We did.

1365
00:58:45.410 --> 00:58:46.010
We really did.

1366
00:58:48.850 --> 00:58:50.270
We built this city.

1367
00:58:50.550 --> 00:58:51.230
We did.

1368
00:58:52.870 --> 00:58:59.110
That was the song that we couldn't wait to come on at the Mixers when I was in 7th and 8th grade.

1369
00:58:59.290 --> 00:58:59.410
Yeah.

1370
00:59:00.750 --> 00:59:01.450
All right.

1371
00:59:02.310 --> 00:59:10.290
Well, we're basically going to go now from a five-minute musical performance to a 10-minute cartoon.

1372
00:59:10.530 --> 00:59:11.790
Well, here's what happened.

1373
00:59:12.030 --> 00:59:14.550
You know, Lumpy, he kind of growls at a guard.

1374
00:59:14.550 --> 00:59:17.270
And the stormtrooper's like, really mean.

1375
00:59:17.430 --> 00:59:19.110
They shove Itchy to the ground.

1376
00:59:19.270 --> 00:59:20.530
Lumpy starts freaking out.

1377
00:59:20.650 --> 00:59:22.990
The general says, keep them quiet or else.

1378
00:59:23.490 --> 00:59:23.970
Yeah.

1379
00:59:24.190 --> 00:59:24.950
Or else what?

1380
00:59:25.430 --> 00:59:28.590
So Mala puts on one of Lumpy's favorite cartoons.

1381
00:59:28.810 --> 00:59:30.210
The stormtrooper walks over.

1382
00:59:30.290 --> 00:59:31.490
He's like, what's this all about?

1383
00:59:31.750 --> 00:59:35.470
And then quickly, Lumpy pretends to be playing like a video game.

1384
00:59:35.470 --> 00:59:39.590
And then when he walks away, it cuts to he's watching this cartoon.

1385
00:59:39.910 --> 00:59:44.670
Why he couldn't know that he's watching a cartoon, I don't know.

1386
00:59:44.810 --> 00:59:45.830
It's about the resistance.

1387
00:59:46.250 --> 00:59:46.950
That's probably why.

1388
00:59:47.190 --> 00:59:48.050
Oh, so maybe it's like, right.

1389
00:59:48.310 --> 00:59:54.370
But while he's watching the cartoon, the stormtroopers are going to supposedly search the residence.

1390
00:59:54.670 --> 00:59:56.150
How big is the residence?

1391
00:59:56.150 --> 00:59:58.390
I can see the whole bottom floor.

1392
00:59:58.390 --> 01:00:00.690
And when they go upstairs, it looks like one bedroom.

1393
01:00:00.870 --> 01:00:03.070
It's just Lumpy's room up there.

1394
01:00:03.350 --> 01:00:03.670
It's not that large.

1395
01:00:04.250 --> 01:00:08.390
When the cartoon came on, it's called The Faithful Wookiee.

1396
01:00:08.410 --> 01:00:09.710
And I didn't watch it.

1397
01:00:09.910 --> 01:00:11.270
I watched the whole thing.

1398
01:00:11.430 --> 01:00:14.910
I just, I just, I couldn't watch it.

1399
01:00:15.310 --> 01:00:16.050
I watched it.

1400
01:00:16.150 --> 01:00:18.270
It's much better than the holiday special.

1401
01:00:18.610 --> 01:00:18.830
Truly.

1402
01:00:19.250 --> 01:00:21.630
If you're going to watch anything, just watch this.

1403
01:00:21.630 --> 01:00:29.310
Well, according to the Nielsen data, you can see that the ratings for the special fall off after the cartoon.

1404
01:00:30.070 --> 01:00:32.930
People stayed for the cartoon and then they were like, I'm out.

1405
01:00:33.110 --> 01:00:36.810
You can find just the cartoon on YouTube now and you don't have to watch the special.

1406
01:00:37.130 --> 01:00:39.370
But basically, I'll sum it up for you.

1407
01:00:39.950 --> 01:00:44.370
Luke Skywalker, C-3PO, and R2-D2, they're searching for a talisman.

1408
01:00:44.630 --> 01:00:50.290
And the Millennium Falcon crashes on the water moon of Pana with the main characters on board.

1409
01:00:50.290 --> 01:00:58.250
Then they run into Boba Fett, who saves Luke from a giant monster and he claims to be there to help them.

1410
01:00:58.370 --> 01:01:00.890
But as it turns out, he's actually working for Darth Vader.

1411
01:01:01.370 --> 01:01:02.750
Well, here's a fun fact.

1412
01:01:02.950 --> 01:01:07.030
This cartoon introduced the character of Boba Fett to the Star Wars universe.

1413
01:01:07.390 --> 01:01:09.370
Well, some might think that.

1414
01:01:10.730 --> 01:01:16.450
But yes, it introduced everyone to Boba Fett in a television medium, on a screen.

1415
01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:25.830
But some fans might be surprised to know that the very first proper public appearance of Boba Fett wasn't on the big screen or even on TV.

1416
01:01:26.670 --> 01:01:32.230
Boba first appeared at a parade for the San Asilmo County Fair in September of 1978.

1417
01:01:33.790 --> 01:01:35.050
He was in a parade.

1418
01:01:35.450 --> 01:01:39.050
Before he was ever on screen, he was in a parade.

1419
01:01:39.050 --> 01:01:41.270
How did anyone know who he was?

1420
01:01:42.210 --> 01:01:43.650
How did he end up in the parade?

1421
01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:51.570
Well, I will tell you, there is a documentary called Under the Helmet, The Legacy of Boba Fett on Disney Plus, and it talks all about it.

1422
01:01:51.830 --> 01:01:52.130
Huh.

1423
01:01:53.050 --> 01:01:54.510
Well, there you go.

1424
01:01:55.530 --> 01:02:01.270
So, I have a question about the cartoon, because I did watch a little bit of it, and I am trying to wrap my head around it.

1425
01:02:01.410 --> 01:02:09.350
So, what's happening is, Lumpy is watching a cartoon about his actual dad.

1426
01:02:09.570 --> 01:02:13.150
Yeah, his dad must be famous, because his dad is Han Solo.

1427
01:02:13.150 --> 01:02:14.150
He's been made into a cartoon.

1428
01:02:14.490 --> 01:02:14.790
Yeah, mm-hmm.

1429
01:02:15.210 --> 01:02:15.610
Okay.

1430
01:02:15.830 --> 01:02:16.750
He loved it.

1431
01:02:16.910 --> 01:02:17.250
Mm-hmm.

1432
01:02:17.830 --> 01:02:25.670
Now, we're going to cut back and see that the Wookiee home is just being completely destroyed by the troopers and this officer.

1433
01:02:26.210 --> 01:02:27.610
They found nothing.

1434
01:02:28.270 --> 01:02:32.910
They've trashed Lumpy's room, and then the officer is like, clean up your room.

1435
01:02:33.150 --> 01:02:33.870
Ha, ha, ha.

1436
01:02:34.030 --> 01:02:37.390
I think it's hilarious to trash a child's room.

1437
01:02:37.550 --> 01:02:38.410
So funny.

1438
01:02:38.790 --> 01:02:44.070
They discover that Lumpy's stuffed animal, which was a bantha, had been decapitated.

1439
01:02:44.250 --> 01:02:45.330
Well, they ripped his head off.

1440
01:02:45.330 --> 01:02:45.910
I know.

1441
01:02:45.910 --> 01:02:47.390
Oh, they're jerks.

1442
01:02:48.170 --> 01:02:51.870
Lumpy is now going to, for a reason I didn't understand.

1443
01:02:52.050 --> 01:02:52.670
I don't get it.

1444
01:02:52.810 --> 01:02:59.290
He's going to watch an instructional video on how to rebuild his mini transmitter.

1445
01:02:59.670 --> 01:03:04.830
You kind of just have to make the jump that the stormtroopers wrecked it, and now he's trying to fix it.

1446
01:03:04.870 --> 01:03:05.490
I guess.

1447
01:03:05.790 --> 01:03:10.670
This is going to be another comedy bit from Harvey Korman.

1448
01:03:11.630 --> 01:03:13.870
This is really just a bunch of physical comedy.

1449
01:03:13.870 --> 01:03:18.930
It's the worst instructional video ever because the person giving it slowly –

1450
01:03:18.930 --> 01:03:20.050
He's a robot.

1451
01:03:20.070 --> 01:03:21.810
He's a robot who slowly shuts down.

1452
01:03:21.810 --> 01:03:22.990
He's like malfunctioning.

1453
01:03:23.070 --> 01:03:24.610
Why would you publish this video?

1454
01:03:24.890 --> 01:03:28.210
If you took this video, it's not live, right?

1455
01:03:28.210 --> 01:03:30.690
It's not a live video, right?

1456
01:03:30.690 --> 01:03:35.990
He's watching a video like if we went on YouTube to be like, how do I fix my dishwasher?

1457
01:03:36.490 --> 01:03:38.710
And the one that you're watching is broken.

1458
01:03:39.070 --> 01:03:41.070
It shorts out as you watch it.

1459
01:03:41.170 --> 01:03:43.850
Yes, the robot instructor keeps shorting out.

1460
01:03:43.930 --> 01:03:45.070
Why would you post it?

1461
01:03:45.310 --> 01:03:50.170
Why wouldn't you get your robot in order before you posted the video?

1462
01:03:51.110 --> 01:03:51.870
I don't know.

1463
01:03:52.350 --> 01:03:52.590
Okay.

1464
01:03:52.590 --> 01:03:56.970
But Harvey Korman does some really funny physical comedy here.

1465
01:03:57.210 --> 01:03:57.370
He does.

1466
01:03:57.570 --> 01:03:58.150
He does.

1467
01:03:58.630 --> 01:04:03.850
Now on the TV, I'm not sure why, but we're transmitted to Tatooine.

1468
01:04:04.230 --> 01:04:06.590
We're at Bea Arthur's bar.

1469
01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:07.710
Akmina.

1470
01:04:08.130 --> 01:04:10.230
Akmina is played by Bea Arthur.

1471
01:04:10.370 --> 01:04:11.690
She runs this bar.

1472
01:04:11.970 --> 01:04:14.250
She's tasked with managing the bar.

1473
01:04:14.370 --> 01:04:15.150
It's very busy.

1474
01:04:15.150 --> 01:04:18.790
And now we have another character played by Harvey Korman.

1475
01:04:19.130 --> 01:04:21.350
His name is Krellman.

1476
01:04:21.830 --> 01:04:27.330
He has six fingers and he drinks liquid by pouring liquid into the top of his head.

1477
01:04:27.650 --> 01:04:31.890
He's going to come over and he's going to order a drink.

1478
01:04:32.030 --> 01:04:37.450
And I just really love Bea Arthur in this scene and I thought we should hear it.

1479
01:04:37.730 --> 01:04:40.510
She's not taking any of his BS.

1480
01:04:41.910 --> 01:04:42.750
What'll I do?

1481
01:04:43.310 --> 01:04:44.610
Hello, Akmina.

1482
01:04:45.350 --> 01:04:46.750
Okay, we'll do it your way.

1483
01:04:46.890 --> 01:04:47.030
Hello.

1484
01:04:47.430 --> 01:04:48.350
Now we'll do it my way.

1485
01:04:48.470 --> 01:04:48.970
What'll it be?

1486
01:04:49.390 --> 01:04:50.070
Can we talk?

1487
01:04:50.890 --> 01:04:52.210
Well, of course we can talk.

1488
01:04:52.350 --> 01:04:53.230
We are talking.

1489
01:04:53.630 --> 01:04:54.670
You're not ordering.

1490
01:04:54.870 --> 01:04:55.690
I'm not pouring.

1491
01:04:55.950 --> 01:04:56.850
We are not drinking.

1492
01:04:57.150 --> 01:04:57.870
We are talking.

1493
01:04:58.470 --> 01:05:03.150
I'm moving this to make room for a drink so that next time I say, what'll it be, and you

1494
01:05:03.150 --> 01:05:04.650
tell me, I can put it right there.

1495
01:05:05.050 --> 01:05:05.530
It doesn't matter.

1496
01:05:05.770 --> 01:05:06.250
Give me anything.

1497
01:05:06.790 --> 01:05:07.550
I'll have one of those.

1498
01:05:09.010 --> 01:05:10.730
I'm sorry I couldn't get back before.

1499
01:05:11.070 --> 01:05:11.730
Before what?

1500
01:05:12.550 --> 01:05:13.230
Until now.

1501
01:05:13.730 --> 01:05:16.810
Until tonight, I thought about it a dozen times, but I had to be sure.

1502
01:05:17.090 --> 01:05:17.710
Excuse me.

1503
01:05:17.790 --> 01:05:18.650
I have a customer waiting.

1504
01:05:18.750 --> 01:05:19.250
I'll be right back.

1505
01:05:20.330 --> 01:05:21.430
Come back soon.

1506
01:05:21.850 --> 01:05:22.870
I'll be waiting.

1507
01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:24.430
I just love her.

1508
01:05:24.490 --> 01:05:27.750
I feel like she's the Joe Bennett of the Star Wars special.

1509
01:05:28.010 --> 01:05:28.670
She is.

1510
01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:31.710
She's like, fine, we'll do it your way.

1511
01:05:31.910 --> 01:05:32.190
Hello.

1512
01:05:32.530 --> 01:05:33.690
Now we'll do it my way.

1513
01:05:33.830 --> 01:05:34.630
What do you have?

1514
01:05:34.910 --> 01:05:35.350
Exactly.

1515
01:05:35.950 --> 01:05:40.890
Well, you know, I read that Bea Arthur's performance by all the critics at the time was singled

1516
01:05:40.890 --> 01:05:43.070
out as a highlight of this holiday special.

1517
01:05:43.150 --> 01:05:44.450
It was the highlight for me.

1518
01:05:44.930 --> 01:05:45.990
This whole section.

1519
01:05:46.170 --> 01:05:47.690
And this was all directed.

1520
01:05:47.850 --> 01:05:51.630
Her whole section, she's about to sing, was directed by the first director.

1521
01:05:51.630 --> 01:05:56.650
And I guess there are some rumors that the shoot was 24 hours.

1522
01:05:56.990 --> 01:05:57.770
Oh my gosh.

1523
01:05:57.830 --> 01:06:00.750
It was a crazy, crazy shoot day.

1524
01:06:00.990 --> 01:06:05.770
I saw in an interview that Bea Arthur said she was cast as Akmina thanks to her friendship

1525
01:06:05.770 --> 01:06:08.890
with Ken and Mitzi Welch, two of the show's producers.

1526
01:06:09.210 --> 01:06:13.210
They also wrote the song, Good Night But Not Goodbye, which is the song that she's going

1527
01:06:13.210 --> 01:06:14.230
to sing in a second.

1528
01:06:14.850 --> 01:06:18.370
Bea Arthur's commitment to the reality of the scene is really incredible.

1529
01:06:18.810 --> 01:06:20.110
She is so fantastic.

1530
01:06:20.110 --> 01:06:24.590
These Imperial Guards are going to come on the screen and they're going to impose a curfew.

1531
01:06:25.470 --> 01:06:27.030
Everyone has to leave the bar.

1532
01:06:27.310 --> 01:06:28.770
Yeah, she said, guys, we're closing.

1533
01:06:28.950 --> 01:06:29.750
They're closing me down.

1534
01:06:29.850 --> 01:06:30.570
You got to leave.

1535
01:06:30.830 --> 01:06:35.670
But everyone saw the Imperial Guard come on the screen and impose this curfew.

1536
01:06:35.810 --> 01:06:37.750
It's not like she took a phone call in the back.

1537
01:06:37.890 --> 01:06:40.410
No, they pop up on a screen like they do.

1538
01:06:40.810 --> 01:06:42.050
But no one will leave.

1539
01:06:42.190 --> 01:06:42.750
They don't care.

1540
01:06:42.970 --> 01:06:43.070
Why?

1541
01:06:43.210 --> 01:06:44.150
Why won't they leave?

1542
01:06:44.290 --> 01:06:44.710
I don't know.

1543
01:06:44.930 --> 01:06:47.170
Why is she the only person afraid of this curfew?

1544
01:06:47.310 --> 01:06:49.410
She's like begging them, you guys, you got to go.

1545
01:06:49.410 --> 01:06:54.690
She's like, I'll give you one more round of drinks and I'm going to sing you a song and

1546
01:06:54.690 --> 01:06:55.790
then you got to go.

1547
01:06:56.130 --> 01:06:56.730
You got to leave.

1548
01:06:57.210 --> 01:06:59.050
She should have put on the holiday special.

1549
01:06:59.890 --> 01:07:00.790
You know what?

1550
01:07:01.030 --> 01:07:02.350
She didn't have it yet.

1551
01:07:02.350 --> 01:07:03.290
She didn't have it yet.

1552
01:07:03.470 --> 01:07:04.430
She didn't know.

1553
01:07:04.990 --> 01:07:06.970
Let me tell you a little bit about Bea Arthur.

1554
01:07:07.510 --> 01:07:09.870
She was an actress, a comedian and a singer.

1555
01:07:09.870 --> 01:07:15.370
She began her career on stage where she won a Tony for playing Vera in Mame.

1556
01:07:15.550 --> 01:07:20.310
So she was really a famous stage actress, musical theater star.

1557
01:07:20.790 --> 01:07:26.310
By the time she did this special, she was very well known for being in the comedy series

1558
01:07:26.310 --> 01:07:29.390
All in the Family and Maud, for which she won an Emmy Award.

1559
01:07:29.730 --> 01:07:32.150
The holiday special was pre-Golden Girls, though.

1560
01:07:32.650 --> 01:07:34.450
Here's a fun fact about Bea Arthur.

1561
01:07:34.450 --> 01:07:39.290
She has received the third most Emmy Award nominations with nine.

1562
01:07:39.930 --> 01:07:41.870
Do you know who's received the most?

1563
01:07:42.570 --> 01:07:43.470
Lucille Ball?

1564
01:07:43.850 --> 01:07:44.310
No.

1565
01:07:45.290 --> 01:07:46.550
Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

1566
01:07:46.650 --> 01:07:47.390
Oh my goodness.

1567
01:07:47.390 --> 01:07:49.250
Has been nominated 11 times.

1568
01:07:49.510 --> 01:07:51.830
